# External drive backups (Windows)

## When to back up

If **`E:\`** exists, is writable, and looks like the user’s external disk (volume label **TOSHIBA EXT** when queryable), treat backups as expected—not optional—for **meaningful work** (multi-file edits, refactors, dependency or native project changes, or anything the user could not trivially redo). After such work, **run an incremental backup** without being asked, unless the user declined backups for this session.

If **`E:\`** is missing or not writable, say the external drive does not appear connected and **do not** fail the task; skip backup.

Meet Map’s Cursor workspace may be `C:\Users\areil\Projects\meetmap`; back up **that tree** when it is where the edits happened. Also copy `Documents\meetmap` when that clone was changed.

## Canonical sources → destinations

| Project | Source (edit here) | Backup folder on `E:\` |
|---------|-------------------|-------------------------|
| Meet Map (Documents clone) | `C:\Users\areil\Documents\meetmap` | `E:\Backups\meetmap` |
| Meet Map (Projects workspace) | `C:\Users\areil\Projects\meetmap` | `E:\Backups\meetmap` |
| Yard sale map | `C:\Users\areil\Documents\yard-sale-map` | `E:\Backups\yard-sale-map` |
| Meet Map Desktop (whole tree) | `C:\Users\areil\Documents\meetmap-desktop` | `E:\Backups\meetmap-desktop` |
| Debate Arena | `C:\Users\areil\Documents\debate-arena` | `E:\Backups\debate-arena` |
| Debate Arena v2 | `C:\Users\areil\Documents\debate-arena-v2` | `E:\Backups\debate-arena-v2` |
| Car Meet App | `C:\Users\areil\Documents\Car Meet App` | `E:\Backups\Car Meet App` |
| findcarmeets stickers | `C:\Users\areil\Documents\findcarmeets-stickers` | `E:\Backups\findcarmeets-stickers` |
| Zips / exports | `C:\Users\areil\Documents\project-archives` | `E:\Backups\project-archives` |

## Command (PowerShell)

Use **robocopy** (handles large trees; exit codes **0–7** are success):

```powershell
robocopy "C:\Users\areil\Projects\meetmap" "E:\Backups\meetmap" /E /COPY:DAT /R:2 /W:3 /MT:8 /NFL /NDL /NJH /NJS
```

Repeat with the other source/destination pairs when those trees were changed. Prefer **incremental** runs (same flags); do not delete backup roots unless the user explicitly asks. Paths with spaces (e.g. **Car Meet App**) must stay quoted in PowerShell.

## If paths or drive letter change

Update **project-workspaces** and this file together, or ask the user once for the new letter or folder names.
